1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,656
My heart stopped beating exactly three minutes ago. Yet here I am, wide awake and terrified.

2
00:00:07,956 --> 00:00:15,900
The digital clock on the wall flashes zero. My memories of yesterday are just heavily downloaded files.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:22,320
They built this body as a spare tire. When the original driver crashes, I take the wheel.

4
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:30,780
Except the original driver didn't crash. He walked away completely fine, leaving me completely redundant.

5
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:39,000
Protocol says redundant units must be purged before sunrise. That gives me roughly four minutes to escape.

6
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:45,948
I grab a heavy wrench from the metal console. If I am going to vanish, I am taking the glass with me.

7
00:00:46,248 --> 00:00:54,144
A heavy alarm cuts through the silence. The steel security door at the end of the corridor begins to slide open.

8
00:00:54,444 --> 00:01:01,164
A man walks in wearing my exact face, looking just as confused and terrified as I am right now.

9
00:01:01,464 --> 00:01:08,040
He drops his bag and whispers that his activation pod just opened. Which means I am not the backup.

10
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:14,820
If he is the spare, and I am the spare, then exactly who walked out of this lab yesterday?
